Three significant elements constitute trafficking:
(a) The action involving recruitment and transportation;
(b) The means employed such as force, coercion, fraud or deception including abuse of power and bribes; and (c) The preliminary purpose being of exploitation including prostitution, etc.

The forms and purposes of child trafficking may be:-
 (a) Bonded labour;
 (b) Domestic work;

(c) Agricultural labour;
